 2. 🌴 Scoop: GOP&#x27;s surprise South Carolina fear 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Photo illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios. Photo: Sam Wolfe/Bloomberg via Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The Senate Leadership Fund, the main super PAC backing GOP Senate candidates, will inject $5 million into South Carolina as an "insurance policy" for GOP nominee Darline Graham, Axios' Marc Caputo and Alex Isenstadt write. 

 Why it matters: Republicans' worry about a Senate seat in blood-red South Carolina shows just how bad the political environment is for the party. 🧮 By the numbers: Closer-than-expected polling from two firms that typically survey for Republicans sparked concern last week in GOP circles.

 A survey from Trafalgar showed Graham pulling 43% and Andrews 42%, a statistical tie. InsiderAdvantage produced a poll showing a 1-point race that's essentially tied, with Graham at 46% and Andrews at 45%. Keep reading ... Hans Nichols contributed reporting. 💰 Scoop: Everytown for Gun Safety, a group pushing stricter gun laws, is teaming up with House Democrats on a $10 million ad campaign to boost gun safety advocates running for Congress, Axios' Andrew Solender reports . 

 
 
