 8. 🏀 1 hoop thing: NBA to experiment with smart balls 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The NBA is experimenting with two pieces of technology in the lead-up to the new season , which tips off Tuesday, Oct. 20:

 Some preseason games will include a smart basketball with a Bluetooth sensor that can collect data for future use in real-time officiating decisions. Some officials will also use wrist wearables to communicate with the replay center in designated situations, including replay reviews, scoring changes and clock malfunctions. Go deeper . 

 
 
